; Refuse an attack between actors that share a side bit
;
; The victim is the record in Noun1Record, the attacker the record in
; ActorRecord (both loaded here). If the subject is the player (Subject = 0) and the
; victim has state bit 4 set, that bit is cleared first. Then the state bytes
; (+4) of the victim and the attacker are ANDed over bits 4-6: if they share a
; bit the attack is refused: the routine drops its own return address (so its
; caller returns to its own caller) and clears ActionAllowed. With no shared
; bit it returns normally, Z set. Used by the attack handler #R$9171 and by the
; handler at #R$9065.
; .
; O:F Z set when the attack may go on (otherwise it does not return)
@label=CheckAttackAllowed
c$914A LD IX,($B708)  ;
 $914E LD A,($B6EA)   ; Subject: 0 = the player
 $9151 AND A          ;
 $9152 JR NZ,$915E    ;
 $9154 BIT 4,(IX+$04) ; state bit 4 of the victim
 $9158 JR Z,$915E     ; only the player clears it
 $915A RES 4,(IX+$04) ;
*$915E LD A,(IX+$04)  ;
@isub=AND STATE_SIDE_BITS
 $9161 AND $70        ;
 $9163 LD IX,($B70C)  ; IX := attacker
 $9167 AND (IX+$04)   ;
 $916A RET Z          ;
 $916B POP HL         ; refused: return to the caller's caller
 $916C XOR A          ;
 $916D LD ($B6FB),A   ; ActionAllowed := 0
 $9170 RET            ;
